": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Hi, I saw that there was a previous issue and discussion going over an error building the takeoff_and_landing example. I went through that discussion a few times and I'm still a little confused. (Apologies I'm completely new to PX4 and MAVSDK development). I cloned the most recent version of the repo and got everything setup properly, but I had the same issues when trying to run the takeoff and land example.\r\n\r\nI was able to get it to build and work in simulation when I switched to the older v1.4.3 branch. But I was just wondering if there was something I should do so that I can run the examples with the newest code?\r\n\r\nIt was mentioned that there is a CI system that should keep everything up to date, and I'm wondering if that is something I need to run manually to update the example files? (Apologies - I'm not familiar with how a CI system works). Just wanted to make sure I had everything up to date before I start practicing with my own examples. \r\n\r\nTo put it more concisely: Is there a way to update the example file so that it will build with the newest main code? Or did I misunderstand the discussion regarding the previous issue? \r\n\r\nThanks!", "closed_by": {"login": "JonasVautherin", "id": 2606672, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDY2NzI=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2606672?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin", "html_url": "https://github.com/JonasVautherin", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/subscriptions", "organiza