, "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/luketjones99/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/luketjones99/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2022-12-10T18:17:10Z", "updated_at": "2022-12-10T18:17:10Z", "body": "I was following the instructions on this quickstart guide: https://mavsdk.mavlink.io/main/en/cpp/quickstart.html. I just cloned the latest version of the repository and get all the PX4 sim stuff setup separately then I cd into the examples directory and run:\r\n\r\ncd takeoff_and_land/\r\ncmake -Bbuild -H.\r\ncmake --build build -j4\r\n\r\nThe first cmake call runs properly, but the second one results in the following errors:\r\n\r\n error: no type named 'NewSystemHandle' in 'mavsdk::Mavsdk'\r\n    Mavsdk::NewSystemHandle handle = mavsdk.subscribe_on_new_system([&mavsdk, &prom, &handle]() {\r\n    ~~~~~~~~^\r\n error: no member named 'unsubscribe_on_new_system' in 'mavsdk::Mavsdk'; did you mean 'subscribe_on_new_system'?\r\n            mavsdk.unsubscribe_on_new_system(handle);\r\n                   ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n                   subscribe_on_new_system\r\n/usr/local/include/mavsdk/mavsdk.h:301:10: note: 'subscribe_on_new_system' declared here\r\n    void subscribe_on_new_system(const NewSystemCallback& callback);\r\n         ^\r\n\r\nI was able to get everything running by switching to an old branch and then re running the cmake lines, and then running:\r\n\r\nbuild/takeoff_and_land udp://:14540\r\n\r\nBut, I figured if I was having to switch to an old branch to get something working, then I was doing something wrong.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/1345353688/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "http